{"id":"scaffold","parent":"infra-build","ord":"a0","title":"Scaffold","done":"2026-08-09T13:06:54-04:00","desc":"Shipped as PR #56 (squash ee09573).\n- flake + npins (kolu@4d8a668, nixpkgs), Bun, drishti-style workspace, bunfig.toml isolated linker\n- @kolu/* hydrate + check-kolu-deps scripts\n- justfile whose `check` recipe IS the CI DAG (`[metadata(\"ci\")]`, odu-only — the planned GHA wrapper was dropped mid-flight at the human's direction)\n- linux + darwin lanes, bun2nix from juspay/bun2nix#2\n- **Effect wired in from day one:** effect + @effect/platform-node at the kolu pin's exact version (4.0.0-beta.106) with single-copy overrides\n- packages/core shipped a real @kolu/surface + Effect Schema cell exercised by bun test\n- **Stale:** that package is gone as of see-outline (PR #58), which split it into format/store/surface/server/web","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:36-04:00"}
{"id":"hm-module","parent":"infra-build","ord":"a1","title":"Home Manager module #racket-parity","done":"2026-08-10T09:55:14-04:00","desc":"Shipped as PR #64 (squash ea85270), authored by Grok, reviewed by Claude.\n- **Fix:** review caught a clean-stop-lands-failed systemd bug (Effect exits 130 on interrupt; SuccessExitStatus now declares it clean)\n- **Fix:** review also caught a README snippet that did not evaluate\n- **From the racket audit (2026-08-09):** the racket flake shipped a home-manager module running serve as a systemd user service (Linux) / launchd agent (macOS) with dataDir/host/port options\n- Port it for `olai web`","after":["see-outline"],"changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:36-04:00"}
{"id":"logging","parent":"infra-server","ord":"a0","title":"Proper logging #techdebt","done":"2026-08-10T14:55:28-04:00","desc":"Added 2026-08-10 after the chat-agent notice shipped as a bare console line ('no ACP agent configured … so chat is off').\n- **Fix:** log the way kolu does — Effect's structured logging throughout the server (levels, spans/annotations, one consistent format, quiet-by-default with a verbosity switch), replacing the ad-hoc options.log/console.log seam\n- Study kolu's logging setup at the pin and match its shape\n- **Folded in from the sloppiness audit (2026-08-10), same seam:**\n  - serve.ts's fault path calls process.exit(1) from a bare .catch, bypassing the scope finalizers the file itself documents as load-bearing (deliberately untested)\n  - listener.ts still renders a raw String(cause) one file from the Cause.pretty helper built to prevent it\n  - OLAI_ALLOWED_ORIGINS is read inline with no named constant and no docs mention, unlike OLAI_DIST_DIR's exemplary pattern","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:36-04:00"}
{"id":"bun2nix-fork","parent":"infra-build","ord":"a2","title":"Drop the bun2nix fork #techdebt #upstream","done":"2026-08-10T12:13:40-04:00","desc":"Shipped as PR #67 (squash 232e774).\n- Upstream nix-community/bun2nix 2.1.2 turned out consumable without flake-parts; the fork input is gone\n- bun.nix equivalence proven by the bun-nix-fresh lane; darwin fix gained; flake.nix header rewritten to tell the new truth\n- **Filed 2026-08-10, a phase-1 watch item never itemized:** the flake's ONE external input was juspay/bun2nix#2 (the rawflake shape), carried because upstream nix-community/bun2nix's nix layer was flake-parts-shaped and could not be consumed\n- Upstream has since shipped fixes the fork lagged (2.1.2 carried a darwin nixpkgs fix at last check)\n- Re-check upstream's shape; if consumable, re-point and delete the fork dependency — if not, PR upstream the rawflake shape and then re-point","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:36-04:00"}
{"id":"serve-surface-app","parent":"infra-upstream","ord":"a0","title":"Upstream: serveSurfaceApp #techdebt #upstream","done":"2026-08-10T16:49:24-04:00","desc":"SHIPPED 2026-08-10 as PR #78 — olai's half, and the debt is paid: pin past kolu #2137 AND #2144.\n- listener.ts shrank from 321 lines to one serveSurfaceApp call\n  - plus the two decisions the primitive leaves: whose port this is (the EADDRINUSE fallback), and what a listener event sounds like (SurfaceAppEvent mapped onto @olai/log: stale tab Info, refused cross-site origin Warn)\n- **Kept outside the primitive:** the frame cap, now `RPC_MAX_FRAME_BYTES` inside the primitive with no option to move it, so #71 cannot recur\n- **Moved the OTHER way:** the surface runtime's lifetime, into serve.ts, which built it\n- listener.test.ts retargeted off the number onto the sink (real sockets, asserting on what the logger heard)\n- **Pin fallout (bunfig-invariant, not feature):** @kolu/url-shape joins the hydrate list; ws moves to the root manifest and leaves @olai/server; check-kolu-deps.sh grew peerDependencies\n- architecture.md's 'Owed upstream' note now reads 'Paid upstream'\n- **Evidence:** shutdown.test.ts caught the primitive's teardown hanging under bun (server.close's callback registered while a socket was open — node never sees it); that diagnosis went into kolu #2144, and the fence passes against the primitive now\n\nDISPATCHED 2026-08-10 → Kolu terminal e500de76 (Claude/Opus).\n- **PARKED same day:** the primitive's teardown hangs under bun (server.close registered while a socket is open — caught by olai's SIGINT fence); fix folded into the human's in-flight kolu listener-migration PR (kolu #2144); a re-pin past that merge unblocks\n\n**Kolu side SHIPPED 2026-08-10** as kolu PR #2137 (merged by the human):\n- serveSurfaceApp in @kolu/surface-app owns origin gate → upgrade → stale-tab → heartbeat → serve\n- payload cap sourced from the framework constant (unspellable to undercut)\n- 15 e2e tests\n\n**OLAI'S PAYBACK, dispatchable now:**\n- bump the kolu pin past #2137 (just update-pins)\n- delete packages/server/src/listener.ts's hand-rolled sequence in favor of one serveSurfaceApp call\n- shrink/retarget listener.test.ts (the #71 cap test may be subsumed by the primitive's own)\n- update architecture.md's debt note, and done-mark this item\n\n**Original filing:** Pay back the debt architecture.md has carried since phase 2: packages/server/src/listener.ts hand-sequences origin gate → upgrade → stale-tab check → heartbeat → serve, copied from kolu's own surface-app example.\n- PR kolu a serveSurfaceApp primitive owning that sequence; at the next pin bump olai deletes its copy and calls one line\n- Kolu-side work, zero olai conflict\n- (Filed 2026-08-10 — the sloppiness audit flagged this as a prose-only 'for now' with no tracking id)","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:36-04:00"}
{"id":"run-reload","parent":"infra-build","ord":"a3","title":"`just run` auto-reloads on source change","done":"2026-08-11T10:45:01-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-11 on the human's ask. `just serve` watches; `just run` deliberately does not (its comment says so). Wanted: auto-reload on source change for `just run`, with the recipe comment updated to the new truth and the sigint behaviour unregressed. Review waived by the human; evidence is a transcript in the PR description.","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:36-04:00"}
{"id":"precompress-upstream","parent":"upstream-dist-socket","ord":"a0","title":"Upstream: buildSurfaceClient should emit precompressed siblings #upstream","done":"2026-08-12T19:49:20-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-11 from the review of PR #93; the debt had no tracked home, and the convention is that an upstream ask becomes its own node rather than a note in a pull request body. One of the two halves of the parent node's single \"what a built client looks like\" change.\n\n- The fact: kolu's @kolu/surface-app already serves precompressed files when they exist — its freshStaticLayer prefers .br, then .zst, then .gz under the immutable-asset path prefix, falls back to the uncompressed file when none is there, never compresses the HTML shell, and refuses to serve compressed media.\n- But kolu's buildSurfaceClient does not emit those compressed companion files, so every consumer re-invents the post-build step. olai's is packages/web/src/precompress.ts, added in PR #93.\n- The ask: give buildSurfaceClient a precompress option (or make it always on), so the build emits exactly what its own static file server looks for.\n- When it lands: olai deletes precompress.ts.","see":["load-perf"],"changed":"2026-08-27T19:10:28-04:00"}
{"id":"keysbus-upstream","parent":"infra-upstream","ord":"a1","title":"Upstream: kolu re-sent the whole key set for every key added","done":"2026-08-13T19:42:25-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-11 out of PR #95 (snapshot-scale). Both design debates classed it as a plain fix, not a new abstraction.\n\nShipped as kolu PR #2166, merged 2026-08-13: adding M keys within the same tick now costs one keys message and one readAll, where before each added key re-broadcast the entire key set and re-read everything (M times N work); membership changes arriving in the same tick are now merged into one. Tests pin it by failing against the pre-fix server.ts — they expect what used to be 100 messages to be 1 — and the six pre-existing membership-contract tests were left untouched. Reviewed clean by the Grok agent, with a complete durable CI pass on both platforms. olai gets the benefit at its next kolu version bump, riding the re-pin in olai PR #150.","see":["snapshot-scale","surface-mcp-viewing"],"changed":"2026-08-27T19:10:28-04:00"}
{"id":"log-pretty","parent":"infra-server","ord":"a1","title":"Pretty logs on a TTY, logfmt everywhere else","done":"2026-08-11T14:31:06-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-11 from the human's ask (\"improve logging for human-friendliness, retaining agent-friendly format\").\n- Today `@olai/log` emits Effect's logfmt through one logger (`Logger.consoleLogFmt` / `formatLogFmt`, packages/log/src/sinks.ts) on every destination — correct for machines, dense for a human at a terminal\n\n**The design:** split by DESTINATION, not format.\n- When stderr is a TTY: a pretty sink (Effect ships `Logger.consolePretty`: local time, coloured level, message first, key=values dimmed after)\n- When piped / under systemd / in tests: logfmt byte-identical to today — the `@olai/log` testlib decoder and any agent parsing depend on it, so the pretty sink may only exist where no machine reads\n- `OLAI_LOG=logfmt|pretty` forces either way\n- Zero change to `toStdout`/`toStderr` call sites: the TTY check lives inside the sink layer\n\n**Shipped 2026-08-11 in two parts:**\n- PR #97 (squash 87cf89f) landed the split; its review completed post-merge — a process misfire, recorded on the PR itself\n- PR #99 (squash, tip f4ccd3e) carried the findings:\n  - `prettyFor(stream)` reading colour at emit time\n  - Wiring tests for both sinks that mutation-testing proved discriminating (three rounds of \"helper tested, wiring not\" before the lock actually held)\n  - `NO_COLOR`\n  - Per-logger `LogToStderr` scoping\n  - `OLAI_LOG` pinned at every harness spawn site\n  - The knob documented in docs/architecture.md\n","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:36-04:00"}
{"id":"splitting-upstream","parent":"upstream-dist-socket","ord":"a1","title":"Upstream: let buildSurfaceClient turn on code splitting","done":"2026-08-12T19:49:22-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-11 by the orchestrator after the author of the load-perf-p1 work flagged it: an upstream ask with no node of its own is a debt that lives only in prose. One of the two halves of the parent node's single \"what a built client looks like\" change.\n\n- The ask: kolu's buildSurfaceClient should accept a `splitting?: boolean` option — today its call to Bun.build hardcodes it to false. With it, splitting the markdown and syntax-highlighting code off the initial load path (PR #118) would no longer need olai to run a second, hand-written Bun.build and rewrite the HTML shell itself, which is what packages/web/src/markdown.ts does.\n- When it lands: olai deletes most of markdown.ts. Details are in PR #118's description.","changed":"2026-08-27T19:10:28-04:00"}
{"id":"upstream-dist-socket","parent":"infra-upstream","ord":"a2","title":"Upstream: buildSurfaceClient owns what a built client consists of","done":"2026-08-12T19:49:24-04:00","desc":"Agreed in the 2026-08-12 design debate (docs/lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-12.md, entry 1; all three positions signed off). Shipped as kolu PR #2159, squash-merged 2026-08-12, with the paired drishti PR #138 green.\n\n- What was consolidated: the single question \"what does a built surface-app client consist of?\". Both child asks landed together as one change — compressed companion files (.br, .gz, .zst) and the code-splitting option, with the HTML shell never compressed, and skipping or pruning of companion files included.\n- The proof it worked downstream: simply bumping drishti's kolu version turned its uncompressed-only build into one carrying every companion file — its main JavaScript bundle went from 640,266 bytes to 173,165 bytes with brotli — with no change to drishti's own source, which is exactly the point of putting the behaviour upstream.\n- Review by an independent reviewer, one blocking finding: the test named for .zst did not test anything, because deleting the zstd row from the table left the suite green; it was fixed and then verified by deliberately breaking the code to confirm the test fails. The review also flushed out a real gap — the extra-asset fixture sat under the 1024-byte threshold, so growth in companion files was never exercised. The author's refusal to add the ts-pattern dependency was accepted (a Record keyed by the union is used instead, which keeps the paired pull request a pure version bump). A late failure of the ci::e2e-governance check turned out to be an allowlist row for httpDrive.testlib.ts, from the scan for Effect run edges, and was verified by diffing to be governance-only.\n- Noted but not taken: kolu's own vite.config.ts emits .br and .gz but no .zst, even though its server prefers zstd — recorded in the pull request description.\n- olai's side is not this node: at the kolu version bump olai deletes precompress.ts and markdown.ts — the deletion is how the change gets installed. What stays in olai forever: the Solid transform, Tailwind, fonts and icons.","changed":"2026-08-27T19:10:28-04:00"}
{"id":"upstream-readout","parent":"infra-upstream","ord":"a3","title":"Upstream: a connection must not report healthy when a subscription has failed","done":"2026-08-12T19:50:37-04:00","desc":"Agreed in the 2026-08-12 design debate (docs/lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-12.md, entry 2). Shipped as kolu PR #2160, squash-merged 2026-08-12, with the paired drishti PR #139 green (Linux only, per the macOS rule; drishti has no branch protection at all).\n\n- The bug this pays for: connectSurface(...).status could report `live` while a subscription over the same socket had errored. olai shipped exactly that bug — a dead documents.keys subscription rendered as an empty directory under a green status light.\n- The fix: the reported status now folds in the subscriptions' state, naming which subscriptions stopped when it degrades; \"pending does not degrade\" became the universal default; and `needsReload` is carried through. The status is updated from events rather than recomputed by walking on every read.\n- The division of responsibility held: kolu owns the truth of the five states, the application owns how they look. One deliberate deviation, judged sound by the reviewer: kolu's own client ignores conn.health on purpose — it has a per-member onError policy, documented in wire.ts — so the in-repository proof is the surface-app example rail plus seam tests, not a migration of the HostStatusPip component.\n- Review: no blocking code findings; a dispose test that asserted nothing was still required to be fixed (one standard across the batch) and verified by deliberately breaking the code; two documentation lines that stated the wrong thing were corrected; an assertion about the sibling-prefix status was added. A suggestion to add needsReload to the example rail was declined as unreachable dead UI, since the code path it needs (reloadForUpdate) is retired.\n- olai's migration rides a later version bump, not this node: connection/status.ts shrinks to presentation only — \"the files on disk reach this page\" stays olai's own sentence.","changed":"2026-08-27T19:10:28-04:00"}
{"id":"upstream-chunking","parent":"infra-upstream","ord":"a4","title":"Upstream: kolu owns splitting an oversized upload into frames","done":"2026-08-12T19:25:21-04:00","desc":"Agreed in the 2026-08-12 design debate (docs/lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-12.md, entry 3). Shipped as kolu PR #2158, squash-merged 2026-08-12.\n\n- Why: sending a message larger than the frame limit is not merely a failed call — the ndjson decoder closes the socket with code 1009 and takes down every subscription on that browser tab. So every surface-app that uploads must split its payload, and the arithmetic had already been derived twice in kolu's orbit: in padi's upload.ts, then in olai's surface/src/attach.ts, which copied it \"because re-deriving it is how the same incident happens twice.\"\n- The fix: chunkBase64 plus the envelope and budget helpers now live beside RPC_MAX_FRAME_BYTES, the constant that defines the cap. The arithmetic: base64 expands by 4/3, the JSON envelope adds its own overhead, there is no third expansion, and the chunk size is a multiple of 3 so every 4-character base64 group decodes on its own. padi's upload.ts was migrated in the same pull request, so the first copy is gone.\n- The boundary held (the Grok agent's proposal, all three debaters signed): content policy stayed in olai — attachmentRejection, the allowed file types, MAX_ATTACHMENT_BYTES and the temporary-directory rule.\n- Review by an independent reviewer, one blocking finding: frameBytesFor was never exercised, so deliberately breaking it left all 56 property tests green; it was fixed and then verified by breaking it both ways. The review also caught that the old 26 MB fixture's expected value was not legal base64, because of a misplaced rounding-up. A paired drishti pull request was judged unnecessary, the change being purely additive. CI: 48 of 48 required checks green on both platforms.\n- Still owed here: olai's attach.ts drops its own arithmetic onto the shared helpers at the next kolu version bump — a separate piece of work.","changed":"2026-08-27T19:10:28-04:00"}
{"id":"kolu-pin-sockets","parent":"infra-upstream","ord":"a5","title":"Adopt the three upstream changes: bump the kolu version and delete olai's copies","done":"2026-08-12T21:28:58-04:00","desc":"olai's half of the three changes agreed in the lowy-electricity design debate, all riding one kolu version bump. Shipped as PR #129 (commit d5b302c), squash-merged 2026-08-13: 30 files, 563 lines net removed.\n\n- Build output: precompress.ts and markdown.ts deleted; build.ts now composes buildSurfaceClient's own precompression and code splitting; .zst files are finally emitted (for the 700 kB entry: 189 kB brotli, 199 kB zstd, 225 kB gzip); the markdown chunk is one literal dynamic import, and the first paint still never fetches it.\n- Connection status: status.ts shrank to presentation only; the client.health() walk, `unhealthy`, `readoutOf` and `needsReload` all left; olai reads conn.readout itself, since kolu's client deliberately does not adopt it automatically.\n- Upload chunking: attach.ts's block of derived constants was replaced by kolu's frame-chunking helpers, imported where they are used; olai's content checks stayed whole.\n- Review: one blocking finding (the orchestrator's own — a roadmap node still naming a deleted file, resolved in this round) plus three suggestions, all taken, with the diff re-verified against the review. Both attempts to sabotage the tests were caught.\n- Beyond the brief: encoding.test.ts now drives every row of kolu's PRECOMPRESSED_ENCODINGS, with the .zst case checked by deliberately breaking it.\n- Filed as its own node from this work: modulepreload-upstream (a 1.5 kB shared chunk with no preload hint). The chunk being named pipeline-<hash>.js rather than markdown-[hash].js is asserted loudly by the end-to-end tests.\n- CI: nine Linux checks green at the final commit, and GitHub reported the branch clean; macOS skipped per the standing rule.","changed":"2026-08-27T19:10:28-04:00"}
{"id":"modulepreload-upstream","parent":"infra-upstream","ord":"a6","title":"Upstream: buildSurfaceClient emits modulepreload for the entry's static chunks #upstream","done":"2026-08-13T11:25:26-04:00","desc":"Shipped as kolu PR #2163 (squashed as e7f0391, merged with admin rights past the failing macOS check on the human's approval, 2026-08-13).\n- buildSurfaceClient now follows the static import edges in Bun's build metafile, transitively, and splices modulepreload link tags into the HTML shell. Dynamic import edges are never followed, and an entry built without code splitting comes out byte-identical.\n- Measured on a simulated Slow 3G connection: the JavaScript critical path went from 6110 ms to 4095 ms.\n- The Grok agent's review approved it, and all three of its suggestions were taken.\n- olai collected the change in PR #139 (squashed as d7cf177): the built shell now carries the preload hint for the entry's shared chunk, verified in the build output before merging. The loop opened by PR #129 is closed.\n- drishti took the same version bump in srid/drishti PR #140 (squashed as dfcb26e), 12 of 12 CI checks green on a re-run; the first run's typecheck failure was a workspace hydration hiccup — @kolu/solid-pwa-install was not visible on that machine, while it was fine locally and on the re-run.\n- All three repositories are now on kolu commit e7f0391.","changed":"2026-08-27T19:10:28-04:00"}
{"id":"owed-moves","parent":"infra-model","ord":"aA","title":"Three small moves: one home for GitState, scale.ts into theme/, and wire.ts using kolu's URL helper","done":"2026-08-13T14:33:36-04:00","desc":"Three small debts agreed in the 2026-08-13 lowy-electricity design debate (items 3, 5 and 6). Shipped as PR #143 (squashed as 9bd7048) on 2026-08-13.\n\n1. GitState is now declared once, in format/src/committing.ts beside RepoState. The reviewer compared the deleted duplicates field by field against the new declaration. It is re-exported from the surface package, so no consumer changed, and the GIT_OFF flag travelled with it. A public export from the ops package that nothing imported (verified to have no importers on master) was dropped.\n2. scale.ts moved into theme/, with every path reference followed: the build, the CSS banner, tests, fixtures and the README.\n3. wire.ts lines 36-39 were deleted — the dial now calls the pinned kolu's `surfaceWsUrl(location.origin)` lazily, as a function rather than a value computed at import time. Laziness was verified (importing the module reads no `location`) and the resulting URLs were checked to match across real origins.\n\nTests pinning the claims: that the text `connectSurface(` appears only in wire.ts — probed in both directions so the test cannot pass vacuously — and that no client file outside connection/status.ts spells the connection status's raw state names.\n\nProcess: reviewed by the Grok agent with no blocking findings, and the claim of zero behaviour change held. The suggestions were taken (three READMEs follow the moved files; a regular expression was widened), and the diff was re-verified against the review twice. Then PRs #141 and #142 landed and master was merged in, with one real conflict in chat/Entry.tsx where both sides were preserved, and the claims sweep extended over #141's new files. CI passed 10 of 10 at commit dba732a on the kolu-ci-1 runner. The author also caught and discarded a first CI attempt that reported green while producing no durable artifacts, re-ran it, and verified the result against the per-step logs.","changed":"2026-08-27T19:10:28-04:00"}
{"id":"fault-root-upstream","parent":"infra-upstream","ord":"a7","title":"Upstream: a throw must not be a white tab — kolu takes a required `fault` #upstream","done":"2026-08-13T16:36:24-04:00","desc":"Agreed in the 2026-08-13 design debate (item 4); the human approved every pull request. Fully shipped on both sides.\n\nkolu PR #2164:\n- The application's composition root now takes a required `fault` handler, the same way it already takes `retired`.\n- A `thrownText` printer moved upstream, with a rule hardened during review: a message counts as already included only when its first line equals the error's name. The Grok review found that using `includes` dropped short messages hidden behind Safari's stack frames, and the fix was written test-first.\n- The error boundary records the fault to the console before rendering anything.\n\nkolu PR #2165: `connectSurface`'s `url` option became optional, defaulting via `surfaceWsUrl`, and it now raises a named error before allocating anything when there is no `location` — a fix, following position C in the debate.\n\ndrishti took the change at its own master version bump.\n\nolai PR #145 (squashed as 120904b) moved the kolu pin to dad81604:\n- main.tsx's hand-written ErrorBoundary, its recording code and thrown.ts were all deleted — the shell now rides kolu's standalone SurfaceFaultBoundary with `fault={(text) => <Fault text={text}/>}`.\n- Fault.tsx keeps only the appearance, verified pixel-identical (colour and vertical rhythm checked) by injecting a real fault into the packaged binary.\n- wire.ts dropped its `url` line in favour of #2165's default.\n- Along for the ride: undoing.ts takes Apply as an argument, and the Bun test setup gets a stub `location`.\n- Omitting `fault` is now a compile error, verified by deliberately removing it (TypeScript error 2322).\n- The end-to-end test for the blank-tab case now asserts on the heading olai owns and names its failure, instead of merely timing out.\n\nProcess: reviewed by the Grok agent, with one blocking finding — the README described the deleted wiring — and three suggestions, all taken. Re-checking the diff caught one more stale comment. A final sweep confirmed no present-tense mentions of the old arrangement remain. CI green at commit 030b85b on the kolu-ci-1 runner.","changed":"2026-08-27T19:10:28-04:00"}
{"id":"agent-model-pin","parent":"infra-process","ord":"a0","title":"Pin each repo's agent model in config #needs-brainstorm","cancelled":"2026-08-25T15:34:17-04:00","desc":"- Root cause: dispatched work sessions ran a bare `claude` command, which defaulted to the Fable model and burned through the Fable quota.\n- Proven: a per-repository .claude/settings.json naming a model, plus permission bypass, beats the machine default — but hand-writing that file was reverted, because the file is generated by apm, the tooling that produces agent configuration for these repositories.\n- The intended real fix: express the model choice once in apm's source of truth, once these repositories adopt apm (see the apm-adoption node).\n- The interim measure, in force: every session is started with an explicit model flag and permission bypass, verified via /status; the machine default is Opus.\n\nCancelled 2026-08-25 by the human, on the orchestrator's assessment: this became redundant once agents.olai became the operating record. The roster rows in that outline are where \"who runs on which model\" lives, the orchestrator is the only thing that starts sessions and derives every start-up command from those rows, so a configuration file would copy roster facts into a file the board does not govern. What remains — someone forgetting the model flag — is no worse than a stale configuration file, and if it ever needs nailing down, the durable place is a `model` property on each roster row, which is an edit to the board rather than an infrastructure task.","changed":"2026-08-27T19:10:28-04:00","custom":{"apm-gone":"2026-08-24 roadmap review: the desc's \"real fix\" points at apm-adoption, which the human dropped to trash (c04369e8) — the fix needs a new home: either bless the interim spawn flag (--model at the kolu create line, the orchestrator's current practice) as permanent, or name where the pin lives now. #needs-brainstorm stands"}}
{"id":"e2e-parallel","parent":"infra-tests","ord":"a0","title":"The e2e suite runs parallel by default, sized to the machine #techdebt","done":"2026-08-13T20:56:00-04:00","desc":"The human's dispatch, 2026-08-13, from the observation that the ~400-scenario suite ran serial everywhere. **Shipped as PR #153 (squash 823a679f), merged 2026-08-14 on the human's direct order.**\n- \"Just squash merge\" — review and remote CI skipped; the kolu-ci network was down and the change is test-infra.\n- Authored by GROK: parallel by default sized to CPU cores, `CUCUMBER_PARALLEL` stays the override (=1 serial).\n- All active lanes were told to merge master so their local CI e2e legs speed up immediately.\n- **Residual to watch:** the write-path 15s-wait scenario family that flaked under box load today.\n  - If parallelism surfaces it in normal runs, deflaking at the root becomes its own item.","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:36-04:00"}
{"id":"fonts-in-store","parent":"infra-build","ord":"a4","title":"Fonts convert once, in the Nix store — not on every build #techdebt","done":"2026-08-13T23:03:47-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-14 on the human's report.\n- PR #152 had put the seam in the wrong place: `nix/fonts.nix` copied raw TTFs and `build.ts` converted all faces to woff2 on every client build.\n- **MERGED 2026-08-13** (night slate; the human pre-approved the merge): PR #155, squashed at master 9f1e1761.\n  - `woff2_compress` now runs in `@olai/fonts`' package-local `default.nix` (store outputs .woff2 directly, 70 faces).\n  - The client build only copies by name.\n  - `@olai/fonts` owns the catalog (`typefaces.ts`), the sheet (`css.ts`), `hosted.json` and the derivation; `nix/fonts.nix` deleted.\n- **Grok review:** 0 blocking, 1 nit (~40→70 docs figure, fixed in 5f113a3).\n- **Evidence** verified independently by the reviewer: store-vs-dist hashes identical, an independent reconversion byte-identical, a clean `just build-client` runs 0 conversions.\n- CI: 9/9 required Linux checks green at 5f113a3.","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:36-04:00"}
{"id":"child-receptacle","parent":"infra-server","ord":"a4","title":"One shared owner for subprocesses: @olai/child #human","done":"2026-08-24T18:00:47-04:00","desc":"- Inventory refreshed 2026-08-24 by the orchestrator, checked against master: of the three duplicate implementations the design debate found, only chat/pipes.ts is still on master. recall/embedder.ts is gone — the recall package now lives only in the parked semantic-recall working tree, and it should consume @olai/child when it returns rather than carry a copy. @kolu/detect's private copy is an upstream file, so unifying that one would be a kolu pull request and is out of scope here.\n- But the duplication is wider than the debate saw: today's subprocess owners are chat/pipes.ts, chat/kolu.ts, git's runner (git.ts, freshly gated per handle by PR #360), format/committing.ts, server/serve.ts, server/edit.ts, main.ts, and web/build.ts — each with its own spelling of spawning, failure, stderr and killing. The weekend's flaky-test campaign (PRs #359, #361 and #364) traced three separate families of test race to exactly this ad-hoc subprocess plumbing.\n- The plan: a workspace package, @olai/child, owning starting a process, a typed execution failure, drained stderr, and killing with a grace period. Explicitly out of scope: readiness, transport, restart policy — and, as an update, sweeping up orphaned processes, which PR #355 answered: the harness reaper and the PDEATHSIG signal own that, and the `kill -9` experiment the debate wanted has been done.\n- To re-verify at dispatch: the swallowed execution error and the graceless kill the debate named (pipes.ts's doc comment still wrestles with an execution error arriving after the spawn), the stale comment, the generic sidecar build under nix/sidecars/<name>/ (motivated by the embedder, so possibly parked with it), and the two embedder tests (parked).\n- Agreed in the 2026-08-14 debate; awaits the human before dispatch.\n\nMerge condition: merge once the pi agent's review has been applied, CI is green, and the orchestrator has checked the list of subprocess owners against the actual diff.","changed":"2026-08-27T19:10:28-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-grok","brief":"briefs/chr.md","dispatched":"2026-08-24T15:52:00-04:00","merge":"merge-auto","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/834fbd45","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/367","worktree":".worktrees/child-receptacle"}}
{"id":"four-way-site-spelling","parent":"infra-model","ord":"a7","title":"\"A place in the loaded set\" is spelled four ways in @olai/format #techdebt","done":"2026-08-15T17:30:07-04:00","desc":"Found during PR #170's refactoring round (2026-08-14), with both reviewers agreeing: the pair `{file, line}` was written four different ways in @olai/format.\n\n- Handed to the human 2026-08-15: PR #188 at commit 5f92af7e, CI 9 of 9 green — and the four turned out to be six, because the pull request also found an inline return type in validate.ts and a web component literally named Site that hand-rolled the same pair.\n- There is now one `Site` type, in node.ts.\n- The point of the change was proven both ways: adding a field now breaks all seven packages and lands on every carrier at once; before, it reached only one of the four spellings.\n- The package's public surface went from 150 to 151 exports, with Site deliberately reachable; behaviour is byte-identical, verified by printing the export keys.\n- Reviews by the Grok and opencode agents: no blocking findings, and neither found a seventh spelling. Two documentation nits were taken — the index header no longer states a number beside a list that can grow (it was wrong once before, PR #170's \"Eight\"), and it says why.\n- Declined on the record, with the reviewers endorsing it: no ordering comparator for the Site type, for one-and-a-half consumers wanting different shapes.\n- The merge is the human's word.","changed":"2026-08-27T19:10:28-04:00"}
{"id":"read-request-inference","parent":"infra-model","ord":"a9","title":"Read tools: TypeScript cannot infer their argument types, so every one spells them by hand #techdebt","done":"2026-08-17T22:27:25-04:00","desc":"Pre-existing, surfaced during PR #170 (2026-08-14): at ops/tools.ts:188 the request half's union Schema.Codec&lt;A,never,never,never&gt; | Schema.Top defeats inference of A, so every read tool hand-annotates its args. The answer half infers since #170. Either a tighter union or a second signature; small type-level work, no runtime change.","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:36-04:00","custom":{"pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/230"}}
{"id":"outlines-quadratic","parent":"infra-model","ord":"a6","title":"outlines() walks O(files × nodes), three passes per file #techdebt","done":"2026-08-15T21:57:00-04:00","desc":"Pre-existing, surfaced during PR #170 (2026-08-14): ops/query.ts:333's outlines() is O(files × nodes) with three passes per file. Untouched by #170 (out of its scope, both reviewers concurred). Matters as vaults grow; one pass with per-file accumulation is the obvious shape, measured before/after when taken.","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:36-04:00","custom":{"pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/198"}}
{"id":"bun-watcher-bump","parent":"infra-build","ord":"a6","title":"File watching costs one fd per file — bun 1.3.14 fixes it #human","done":"2026-08-24T18:03:44-04:00","desc":"- Bun 1.3.13's file watcher opens one file descriptor per file under the watched root: 2055 of them on a git-shaped corpus, half for files olai never reads. Bun 1.3.14 watches per directory instead, taking that from 1050 down to 15, and also fixes a blind spot where directories created after startup were not watched.\n- Verified across the version change: all nine kinds of file change still produce their events, and the full test suite passes on both versions.\n- Options, priced: wait for the new Bun to reach nixpkgs (recommended — no risk, unknown date); override Bun now, which means forking the runtime; write our own watcher (not recommended); or poll, which an earlier ruling forbids.\n- The full pricing is in docs/brainstorming/watcher-fd-cost.md.\n\nMerge: pre-approved by the human on 2026-08-24 at about 16:52 (it had been marked manual) — the orchestrator merges once the pi agent's review has been applied and CI is green, with nothing further to ask.","changed":"2026-08-27T19:10:28-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-grok","brief":"briefs/bwb.md","dispatched":"2026-08-24T16:32:00-04:00","merge":"merge-human","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/fb3a0cfc","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/368","worktree":".worktrees/bun-watcher-bump"}}
{"id":"olai-extension","parent":"infra-model","ord":"a0","title":"Outlines are .olai files: the .jsonl extension retires","done":"2026-08-15T11:35:30-04:00","desc":"Agreed 2026-08-15 (docs/brainstorming/orchestrator.md, question 3): a pure rename, done as a hard cutover with a manual `git mv`; this repository migrates in the same pull request.\n\nProgress as of 2026-08-15:\n- Running in Kolu terminal 939eb88c (Claude Opus, unattended), branch `olai-extension`, PR #177.\n- Delivered:\n  - docs/roadmap.olai and docs/Archive.olai renamed with `git mv`, contents byte-identical.\n  - A constant, OUTLINE_EXT, carries the rule: code that decides reads the constant, prose that describes it spells the extension out — a disagreement between the two reviewers, settled on the record.\n  - A guard test, tests/extension.test.ts, sweeps every path tracked by git for `.jsonl`, both as a string and as a filename, with six named exemptions, each proven to catch a deliberately introduced violation.\n  - Its own review round caught that the sweep read only packages/ and choked on gitignored screenshots; switching to `git ls-files` fixed both.\n- Stage: in review — the Grok agent (terminal 5f4fbcb7) and the opencode agent (terminal 990a07e9), briefed to hunt for spellings the guard test cannot reach and to verify the end-to-end suite really exercises .olai fixtures, the failure mode being that it silently does nothing.\n- Note about parallel work: if PR #175 lands first, this branch re-runs after rebasing and the guard test catches #175's new .jsonl spellings — the guard working as designed.\n- Merge: autonomous once the review is clean and CI is green (the human's ruling).\n- Operational note for the merge: every running olai server — including the orchestrator's own ledger over MCP — keeps reading .jsonl until restarted, so the ledger goes quiet between merge and restart, and the human's other vaults must be renamed by hand (the README carries the `mv` command).\n- Deferred work filed as its own nodes: stem-strippers-twins, and tree-sweep-fixture, which also carries a question for the human about a documentation path.","changed":"2026-08-27T19:10:28-04:00"}
{"id":"stem-strippers-twins","parent":"infra-model","ord":"a8","title":"Two functions strip an outline filename's extension with opposite rules — unify them #techdebt #deferral","done":"2026-08-17T16:00:22-04:00","desc":"Found by PR #177 (2026-08-15), pre-existing: message.ts:148 and dates.ts:387 both strip an outline's suffix, with opposite stated arguments (spell the suffix vs find it). Unifying them needs its own argument. Related micro-fact from the same sweep: node.ts:253's isArchived allocates a string per call on a per-file-per-probe path.","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:36-04:00","custom":{"from":"177","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/227"}}
{"id":"tree-sweep-fixture","parent":"infra-tests","ord":"a4","title":"Three tests each walk the whole repo tree their own way — share one walker when a fourth appears #techdebt #deferral","done":"2026-08-17T16:00:24-04:00","desc":"Counted by PR #177 (2026-08-15).\n\n- acp/manifest.test.ts:76, the claims sweeps, and now tests/extension.test.ts each walk the whole tracked tree their own way.\n- **Rule** (the author's own): a shared fixture is the right move at four, not three — this node exists so the fourth sweep triggers it instead of becoming the fourth spelling.\n- **Also owed a human call**, recorded here rather than lost: docs/RCA/2026-08-11-roadmap-stamp-reverts.md:64 still names docs/roadmap.jsonl inside a dated, explicitly-unbuilt proposal — correct the path or let the dated document stand as written.","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:36-04:00","custom":{"from":"177","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/227"}}
{"id":"pr-body-wrap","parent":"infra-process","ord":"a3","title":"PR: repo markdown unwraps — one line per paragraph, 80 columns stays for source comments","done":"2026-08-15T14:47:49-04:00","desc":"Filed 2026-08-15 from the human's root-cause exchange with one of the work sessions: agents hard-wrapped pull request descriptions at about 80 columns because the repository's own docs/*.md files do — the habit is inherited from the corpus.\n\n- The fix targets the source: unwrap the repository's markdown prose (README, docs/*.md, the brainstorming notes, package READMEs) to one line per paragraph. Code blocks, tables and ASCII diagrams are untouched, and the rendered output is identical. The convention is written into HACKING.md: markdown prose never hard-wraps; the roughly 80-column limit stays for source code comments.\n- Pull request descriptions themselves were explicitly out of scope — the human's correction mid-dispatch, since the habit dies at the corpus, not by editing history.\n- As of 2026-08-15: the Grok agent working alone (terminal 3e7619c0, branch `pr-bodies-unwrapped`), review waived, handed over once green. The scope correction was sent mid-task and acknowledged by the agent's behaviour rather than in words; the diff is whitespace-shaped, so it rebases trivially under whichever sibling pull request lands second.","changed":"2026-08-27T19:10:28-04:00"}
{"id":"quote-safe-selectors","parent":"infra-tests","ord":"a1","title":"PR: e2e steps should build their data- attribute selectors through one quote-safe helper #techdebt #deferral","done":"2026-08-17T16:00:24-04:00","desc":"Filed at PR #182's close (2026-08-15), opencode's nit answered-not-fixed with the receipt on the record.\n\n- Solid sets dynamic attributes via setAttribute so the DOM is escaped by construction — this is a test-selector concern only.\n- data-from was the fourth instance of one house idiom (data-path, data-file, data-node-id).\n- Hardening only the newest made the suite inconsistent for zero coverage.\n- **Fix:** one quote-safe helper across every data- step in packages/tests/step_definitions/.","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:36-04:00","custom":{"from":"182","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/227"}}
{"id":"html-memory","parent":"infra-model","ord":"a5","title":"PR: .html bodies stop living whole in the set — big pages want lazy bodies or a cap","done":"2026-08-16T12:55:44-04:00","desc":"Deferral from PR #189 (2026-08-15).\n\n- Every .html body is held in the loaded set for the process lifetime (ops/codec.ts:44, format/set.ts:53).\n- Saved pages are megabytes with assets inlined — resident memory scales with vault content, no eviction, no cap.\n- Named in docs/format.md:122.\n- **Fix direction:** bodies loaded on read (the snapshot-scale precedent — documents already stopped riding the first frame once) or a size-gated claim that refuses in words.","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:36-04:00","custom":{"pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/204"}}
{"id":"siblings-of-quadratic","parent":"model-indices","ord":"Zz","title":"Step 1: give the derived view real indexes, so scans become lookups","done":"2026-08-16T12:30:00-04:00","desc":"Ruled 2026-08-16: docs/brainstorming/model-indices.md commits to direction C — when a file changes, patch the in-memory view instead of rebuilding it three times per edit, the approach the emanote project uses.\n\n- Direction C lands in four shippable steps; this node is step 1, giving the `Derived` view real indexes:\n  - `byFile` (a file to its nodes), which kills every by-file scan: `siblingsOf`, `nodesOf`, the trash page and the per-candidate loops.\n  - Plus the reverse maps the later patcher needs: `mirrorsOf` (a target to the mirrors resolving to it) and `edgesTo` (a target to the sources whose after/blocks edges land on it).\n  - Built in the same single pass as today's tables, with every scanning site converted to read an index.\n  - This step still rebuilds everything on every edit.\n- Steps 2 to 4 — computing the view once per edit, the patcher with its property test, and sending patches over the wire — become their own roadmap items when the human says to dispatch them.\n- The library survey is concluded: hand-written Maps, no dependency. d2ts and TanStack DB are the productized form of the same ideas, but the wrong size of bite.\n- The Grok agent's warning on PR #198 about a \"blind\" shared grouping helper is answered by putting the grouping inside `Derived`, where it is always paired with its revision.","created":"2026-08-15T21:31:01-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:11:35-04:00","custom":{"pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/205"}}
{"id":"viewport-helper-promotion","parent":"infra-tests","ord":"a2","title":"viewport() joins OlaiWorld — nine step files spell it inline #techdebt","done":"2026-08-16T09:17:25-04:00","desc":"Filed from PR #197's deferral (2026-08-15): the e2e world's own convention says a helper belongs on OlaiWorld once three or four features ask; nine step files spell viewport() inline. Converting them was six files outside #197's diff. Mechanical.","created":"2026-08-15T21:43:03-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:36-04:00","custom":{"pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/200"}}
{"id":"drawnorsaid-extra-frame","parent":"infra-tests","ord":"a3","title":"drawnOrSaid waits one extra frame on the happy path — grok's #199 follow-up #techdebt","done":"2026-08-16T09:17:27-04:00","desc":"Filed from the Grok agent's review of PR #199 (2026-08-16): the one follow-up it would take. The end-to-end test helper `drawnOrSaid` should wait one extra animation frame on its success path, so that a check driven by the mouse and one driven by the keyboard agree about when the tab has finished offering the way back. Small — a precision fix in the end-to-end harness.","created":"2026-08-15T23:47:10-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:11:35-04:00","custom":{"pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/200"}}
{"id":"model-indices","parent":"infra-model","ord":"a4","title":"Model indices: patch the view instead of rebuilding it","done":"2026-08-21T21:43:09-04:00","desc":"- Plan of record (docs/brainstorming/model-indices.md): a small edit costs what it touched, not three whole-corpus rebuilds. From-scratch derive() stays as the oracle a property test holds the patcher to.\n- All four slices shipped (children); the remaining follow-ups are tracked as their own nodes.","created":"2026-08-16T11:11:04-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T21:43:09-04:00","custom":{"closed":"2026-08-21 — the parent mark reconciled: all four slices (#205/#208/#211/#223) and the three deferrals (#218, bench harness, byId overlay) were already done; the one remaining narrowing lives as perf-validate-incremental"}}
{"id":"model-indices-2","parent":"model-indices","ord":"a0","title":"Slice 2: compute the view once per edit — validate's Derived flows through to publish","done":"2026-08-16T15:51:51-04:00","desc":"Thread the already-validated view through to the publishing step, instead of recomputing it over the whole corpus — which is today's second full rebuild. (In the design document docs/brainstorming/model-indices.md this used to be called direction B; it is now the plumbing that direction C needs.) Question 4 of that document — serving derived facts through Surface's derived.collection reconciler — is a later refinement, not part of this step.","after":["siblings-of-quadratic"],"created":"2026-08-16T11:11:04-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:11:35-04:00","custom":{"pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/208"}}
{"id":"model-indices-3","parent":"model-indices","ord":"a1","title":"Slice 3: the patcher — patch(derived, delta) in format/, held to the derive() oracle","done":"2026-08-17T08:45:18-04:00","desc":"One function beside `derive()` in format/, consuming Surface's collection-delta frame (`{upserts, removes}`).\n- Local updates: byFile, children keys owned by the file, byId with duplicate-claimant promotion.\n- A dirty set from the reverse indexes (mirrorsOf, edgesTo) recomputes only touched status/blocked entries.\n- Cycle checks re-run only when edges/mirrors changed.\n- **Copy-on-write:** a patch returns a NEW Derived, sharing untouched maps.\n- **Safety line:** the oracle property test — `patch(derive(before), delta)` deep-equals `derive(after)` over generated edit sequences, duplicate ids on purpose.\n  - The patcher may bail to full `derive()` on hairy cases.\n- Server uses it; the browser still rebuilds in this slice.","after":["model-indices-2"],"created":"2026-08-16T11:11:04-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:36-04:00","custom":{"pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/211"}}
{"id":"model-indices-4","parent":"model-indices","ord":"a2","title":"Slice 4: the browser joins — the derived memo folds delta frames through the same patcher","done":"2026-08-17T12:06:05-04:00","desc":"- Swap `web/src/client/outlines.ts`'s derived memo from flatten-and-derive() to the patcher, over the delta frames the outlines collection already delivers.\n- **No wire change** — outlines-as-collection already paid that cost.\n- State the mixed per-entry revs contract explicitly in the patcher's contract (same as today, not new unsoundness).\n- If the generic fold-a-collection combinator proves itself olai-free here, offer it upstream to kolu Surface as a small PR (the precompress-upstream route) — a consequence of the design, not a prerequisite.","after":["model-indices-3"],"created":"2026-08-16T11:11:04-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:00:36-04:00","custom":{"pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/223"}}
{"id":"check-targets-index","parent":"model-indices","ord":"a3","title":"checkTargets still walks per node — convert to the reverse index without moving error order #techdebt #deferral","done":"2026-08-17T02:04:15-04:00","desc":"Resolved overnight on 2026-08-17: the conversion turned out to have been done already by PR #208 (step 2), and is held in place by three assertions, two of which fail if the code goes back to walking.\n- PR #218 records this in model-indices.md with the measurement: walking takes 4.0 ms versus 0.40 ms through the index on a clean vault, and 144 ms versus 3.8 ms with 200 unknown references. The larger factor is that the \"did you mean\" suggestion is computed once per unknown id — 25 calls instead of 200.\n- Honest closing note: done by PR #208, measured by PR #218.","created":"2026-08-16T12:17:29-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:11:35-04:00","custom":{"from":"205","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/218"}}
{"id":"watch-set-per-connection","parent":"infra-server","ord":"a3","title":"Bodies stay live by refcount, not a 16-slot guess — the wire learns when a reader leaves #deferral","done":"2026-08-17T20:41:08-04:00","desc":"**Reframed 2026-08-17** after reviewing kolu's watchers (was: \"per-connection LRU?\", #204's deferrals 3–5).\n- The 16-path set in `packages/server/src/bodies.ts` is not file-watching (the store already watches the whole directory) — it decides which OPEN pages get their bodies re-read when a revision touches them.\n- The bound exists only because the wire says when a reader OPENS a key and never says when the last one LEAVES (\"the framework owns subscription lifetime and does not publish it\" — bodies.ts).\n  - So eviction is a guess aged out of an LRU, and sixteen newer opens anywhere silence a still-visible page (stale, never wrong; reopen heals; documented in docs/format.md).\n\n**Kolu's honest shape** (`packages/integrations/io/src/refcounted-dir-watcher.ts`, `packages/integrations/git/src/working-tree-watcher.ts`): refcounted subscription per key.\n- First subscribe installs, every consumer shares, last unsubscribe tears down.\n- No cap, no LRU, no per-connection question, because the leave signal EXISTS.\n\n**The fix:**\n- Expose subscription lifetime on olai's wire (the \"keys-style member for who holds this key\" bodies.ts names as its own replacement), and refcount bodies on it — live for exactly the pages somebody has open, no magic number anywhere.\n- Both documented format.md edges (the silenced page; the birth-announce gap in published.ts) get revisited by the same change.\n- **Superseded:** the original per-connection-LRU idea — it would shrink the blast radius while keeping the guess.","created":"2026-08-16T12:49:38-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:36-04:00","custom":{"from":"204","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/229"}}
{"id":"kolu-create-placement","parent":"infra-upstream","ord":"a8","title":"Upstream: kolu's create-terminal endpoint should demand explicit placement — toplevel or child-of #upstream","done":"2026-08-16T21:20:12-04:00","desc":"**Proposed by the human 2026-08-16**, after the orchestrator drifted into spawning reviewers as top-level terminals when the charter said splits — the default absorbed the mistake silently, and the canvas's hierarchy (who works for whom) quietly flattened.\n\n**The design**, simplified on the human's challenge (\"what interactive CLI?\"): humans create terminals through the kolu web canvas, not the CLI — the CLI's real audience is scripts and agents, exactly the callers that drift.\n- No TTY carve-out, no default anywhere.\n- The padi create endpoint takes a REQUIRED placement — `toplevel | childOf(terminalId)`.\n- The CLI requires exactly one of `--toplevel` or `--parent <id>`, erroring otherwise.\n\n**Scope added by the human same day:** the rule also covers kolu's MCP surface.\n- The create-terminal tool `kolu mcp` offers agents takes the same required placement with no default, refusing a call that omits it — agents over MCP are exactly the script-shaped callers the rule exists for.\n- Migration is one word per script.\n\nA kolu PR, dispatched (lane `kolu-create-placement`).","created":"2026-08-16T14:15:53-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:36-04:00","custom":{"pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/2173"}}
{"id":"kolu-watch-next-cli","parent":"infra-upstream","ord":"a9","title":"Upstream: kolu's idle-terminal nagging (shipped) — the snooze verb was cut and does not exist","done":"2026-08-19T10:57:20-04:00","desc":"Revision 3 of docs/brainstorming/kolu-watch-cli.md designed three pieces: the nag (a quiet terminal \"rings\" until worked, killed, or snoozed), a `kolu snooze` command (silence with a mandatory reason and expiry), and `kolu ring --wait` for the watcher.\\n\\n**What actually shipped — kolu pull request #2181, merged by the human 2026-08-18** (title: \"kolu watch grows up: idle terminals nag until dealt with — no new verbs\", built to revision 5 of the design): the state-based watch and nagging machinery, observed working live. **The snooze record was explicitly left out of scope by that PR's own body — `kolu snooze` does not exist today.** Silencing a known hold is therefore only possible via the watcher's --ignore list, reconsidered at each re-arm.\\n\\nIf a snooze is ever asked for again, carry the flaw the human identified on 2026-08-28: a pure-timer snooze survives the terminal becoming active again, so new work dispatched to a snoozed terminal can stop and wait in silence until the timer expires — the design must make activity cancel the snooze.","created":"2026-08-16T17:18:14-04:00","changed":"2026-08-28T08:40:55-04:00","custom":{"pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/kolu/pull/2181"}}
{"id":"kolu-darwin-unit-fsevents","parent":"infra-upstream","ord":"aA","title":"Upstream: kolu's macOS unit tests always fail, which hides its macOS daemon tests","done":"2026-08-17T00:40:26-04:00","desc":"Surfaced by the author of kolu PR #2173 and ruled \"dispatch\" by the human on 2026-08-16. Two coupled facts:\n- The `ci::unit@aarch64-darwin` check has failed more than 20 times in a row on the petit CI machine (the macOS box), caused by the git FSEvents churn tests under packages/integrations/, and it reproduces byte-for-byte on unmodified master.\n- ci/mod.just declares `daemon: install unit`, so while the unit check is red on macOS the daemon test suites there are skipped — macOS daemon coverage is not exercised at all, and because that failing check is required, PR #2173 had to be merged with `--admin`.\n- Fix: repair the churn tests properly if the failure mode allows (preferred), or skip them on macOS with the reasoning pinned — noting that PR #2172's branch already skips two of them on macOS, so reconcile with that rather than colliding.\n- Success means: the macOS unit check green on master, and the daemon suites running on macOS again.","created":"2026-08-16T21:21:04-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:11:35-04:00","custom":{"pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/2176"}}
{"id":"patch-bench-harness","parent":"model-indices","ord":"a5","title":"Commit the 1,000-file patch-vs-rebuild benchmark as a just leg so the order-of-magnitude figure is reproducible #deferral","done":"2026-08-17T22:38:02-04:00","desc":"Open question 5 of docs/brainstorming/model-indices.md.\n- The slice-3 author measured 2–3ms patched vs 25–40ms rebuilt on a 1,000-file / 21,000-record vault as a one-off.\n- The harness is not in the tree, so README/architecture.md deliberately call it an unreproducible laptop sample.\n- **Fix:** commit the harness with a `just` leg.\n- From PR #211; filed on the human's overnight draft ruling.","created":"2026-08-16T23:15:17-04:00","changed":"2026-08-19T19:01:35-04:00","custom":{"from":"211"}}
{"id":"patch-byid-overlay","parent":"model-indices","ord":"a6","title":"Replace the patcher's new Map(byId) clone — roughly half of every patch — with an overlay or persistent map #deferral","done":"2026-08-17T22:38:02-04:00","desc":"Open question 1 of docs/brainstorming/model-indices.md, now answered with a measurement by the slice-3 author: the byId clone is the dominant remaining cost (~half a patch). The lever is an overlay map or a persistent structure — take it when a bigger vault asks. From PR #211; filed on the human's overnight draft ruling.","created":"2026-08-16T23:15:20-04:00","changed":"2026-08-17T22:38:02-04:00","custom":{"from":"211"}}
{"id":"second-pane","parent":"infra-nav","ord":"a0","title":"The Second Pane — split views: N panes, each a full page, the layout in the URL","done":"2026-08-17T17:56:34-04:00","desc":"Proposed in the artifact \"The Second Pane\" (claude.ai/code/artifact/980a4438-9c7f-4e1b-b5b7-18a647c6b379), researched against Workflowy's native panes and the MultiFlow extension.\n\n**Principles:**\n- A pane is a route (page + zoom + filter) rendering the full page component — no second-class panes.\n- Focus is explicit with a visible ring and all shortcuts/palette/filter acting on it.\n- Links deterministic (click = this pane, mod-click = open right).\n- The whole layout serializes into the URL (share/restore/back-forward).\n- Drag between panes native (one store, no frames).\n- Saved layouts are outline nodes.\n\nDispatched to grok 2026-08-17 on the human's word — draft PR, NO agent reviewers, the human reviews by running the branch.","created":"2026-08-17T10:39:40-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:36-04:00","custom":{"pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/225"}}
{"id":"olai-batch-verbs","parent":"infra-mcp","ord":"a0","title":"MCP writes stop costing one round-trip per fact — add_node children carry the whole record, a batch apply runs many ops in one atomic write, and update writes several fields of one node","done":"2026-08-17T12:39:00-04:00","desc":"From the 2026-08-17 orchestration retrospective: a lane spawn cost ~13 olai MCP calls (1 add_node + 9 set_after + 3 set_prop) because each fact is its own round-trip — and the agent's turn latency, not the server, is the cost.\n\n**One PR, three verbs:**\n- `add_node`'s child shape gains `after`, `see`, and `props` so a captured subtree arrives with its edges and facts in the same atomic write.\n- `apply` — a list of ops executed in order, one validation, one write, one rev, all-or-nothing with the failing op named.\n- `update {id, mark?, desc?, props?, after?}` for the done+sha+note trio.\n\n- Every refusal the single verbs make (shadowed keys, unknown ids with closest match, cycles named, done-over-unfinished from #207), the batch forms must make identically.\n- **Ruled:** auto-merge on clean evidence.","created":"2026-08-17T10:44:55-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:36-04:00","custom":{"pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/224"}}
{"id":"kolu-one-shot-submit","parent":"infra-upstream","ord":"aB","title":"Upstream: send a message to an agent terminal in one call #upstream","todo":true,"desc":"- The ask: `sendInput` grows a submit option and `create` grows a message, so dispatch is one call instead of three.\n- kolu PR #2177 was closed unmerged after field testing: its core premise — output-quiet means prompt-ready — is false (grok's idle TUI repaints defeat any settle window).\n- For the successor: keep the mid-turn refusal semantics, the 30s bound and the recognition work (branch `one-shot-submit` preserved); replace the quiet heuristic with a real agent-state signal — the adapter knows idle, ask it.\n- Related: kolu-watch-next-cli encodes the same lesson for supervision.","created":"2026-08-17T10:44:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T16:04:56-04:00","custom":{"prerequisite-landed":"2026-08-24 roadmap review: the successor's prerequisite shipped upstream — the current pin (82518c4c) carries wait_agentState (working/awaiting/waiting buckets, settledMs conjunct, in-wait screenTail): the \"real agent-state signal\" this node said the one-shot send needs. The ask itself (a submit that cannot race the TUI) is still unlanded (lifecycle_sendInput still documents the three-step protocol; lifecycle_create's run is a shell line, not a message). Unblocked; wants authoring"}}
{"id":"faithful-addresses","parent":"infra-model","ord":"a3","title":"Make addresses mirror the directory: /notes.olai, not /o/notes.olai #needs-brainstorm #human","done":"2026-08-21T21:43:09-04:00","desc":"- The complaint: the /o/ and /doc/ prefixes invent structure the disk doesn't have — the file's own suffix already says what kind of page it is.\n- The sketch: file paths ARE the addresses, and computed pages wear a reserved marker (/:today, /:agenda, /:trash) that can't collide with a filename.\n- Two things a design must answer: collisions (a file literally named `agenda`), and the node permalink (/n/<id> survives moves; any path-carrying form can lie after one).\n- Blocks saved layouts — anything that stores a route bakes in the current spelling. Also touches #225's pane-list URL and its tests.\n- Wanted as a proper system design, not patched address by address.\n\n**pr** — (2026-08-19) — addresses are paths: /Tasks.olai, /notes/README.md#h, /#id for a node, /d/<ISO>, /today, /agenda, /trash; collisions impossible (every served file carries a registry suffix, computed pages spell no file); the node permalink stays location-free. Reconciled 2026-08-21 — the node had been left todo; its one leftover (the bundle collision) is filed in the Inbox as bundle-reserved-prefix from=#256","created":"2026-08-17T18:02:56-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T21:43:09-04:00","custom":{"merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/675886e0","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/256"}}
{"id":"chat-at-nodes","parent":"infra-chat","ord":"a0","title":"Chat: typing @ completes NODES too, not just file paths — hand the agent a task by name","done":"2026-08-17T21:09:49-04:00","desc":"Chosen by the human 2026-08-17 as the next feature.\n- PR #213 gave the chat composer @-completion over FILE paths (server's own prune + kind registry, WeakMap fold, eight rows, tagOpensAt reused so @person habit does not collide).\n- **This is the other half:** the same @ also completes NODES — type `@hinge` and pick the node, so you can say \"look at @pick the hinges\" instead of pasting a path and hoping the agent finds the row.\n- Reuses the completion machinery just built rather than inventing a second one.","created":"2026-08-17T18:05:22-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:36-04:00","custom":{"pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/228"}}
{"id":"mentions-index-one-sigil","parent":"infra-model","ord":"aB","title":"One index for both @mentions and #tags, not just @","done":"2026-08-18T21:55:00-04:00","desc":"Filed at PR #237 by the altitude pass; shipped in PR #249.\n\n- Problem: the mentionedBy index recorded the @ namespace and dropped the leading character, but the fold it rode on (titleParts) was already producing #topic parts and throwing them away — so the index was half a reverse index of tags written in prose.\n- Fix: one `taggedBy` index keyed by the written form, so @herbs and #herbs are two different keys. It was re-keyed in one change across derive.ts, the patcher's taggings(), the oracle's readable() and backlinksOf; the mayHoldSigil helper went with it.\n- web/src/client/complete/tags.ts now reads the index instead of scanning every node of the corpus on every derivation.\n- Measured, which was this deferral's condition — two new `just bench` steps print both halves:\n  - Completion: 18.5 ms scanning versus 0.47 ms reading the index; 12.2 ms of the scan was the title-only walk that already existed, answering 60 tags against the index's 1,052.\n  - Corpus-wide fold: 6.5 ms filing @ alone versus 18.6 ms filing both leading characters.\n  - End to end, interleaved across two working trees: a full rebuild goes from 32.8 ms to 46.7 ms and a one-file patch from 0.67 ms to 0.85 ms, against roughly 18 ms saved on every derivation while a tag is being typed.\n- Verdict: yes, with the cost stated — the saving is per keystroke, the cost is per cold rebuild.\n- Bonus: completion got wider — a tag written in a note is now offered, and the count is one vote per record rather than one per occurrence.","created":"2026-08-18T06:05:00-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:11:35-04:00","custom":{"from":"237"}}
{"id":"olai-convention-dir","parent":"infra-model","ord":"a1","title":"_olai/Trash.olai is the one trash — the archive name dies; Inbox.olai stays top-level","done":"2026-08-19T21:52:16-04:00","desc":"Ruled with #246: minted convention files land in `_olai/` (underscore, not dot — the store prunes dot-directories); `Pins.olai` already mints there.\n\n- **CORRECTED AND EXTENDED by the human 2026-08-19** (supersedes the earlier \"Archive.olai and Inbox.olai follow Pins.olai\" spelling):\n\n1. **There is ONE trash: `_olai/Trash.olai`.**\n   - The per-directory Archive.olai convention dies.\n   - Trashing a node from any outline writes into that one file (an entry must therefore record which outline it came from, so untrashing can put it back).\n2. **Inbox.olai stays top-level** — it does not move into `_olai/`; its by-name resolution and root minting are untouched.\n3. **Full rename, the human's word**: the file, the verbs and the operator all say trash.\n   - `archive_node`/`unarchive_node` become `trash_node`/`untrash_node`; `empty_trash` empties `_olai/Trash.olai`; `is:archived` becomes `is:trashed`.\n   - \"archive\" as a word leaves the product (tools, search grammar, web faces, docs).\n   - BREAKING for agents; blessed.\n4. **Existing per-directory Archive.olai files are left on disk and STOP being read**: no longer trash, not drawn on the trash page, invisible to `is:trashed` — orphaned until a human hand-moves them.\n   - No migration in this PR.\n\n- **Docs to sweep:** format.md, architecture.md wherever Archive.olai is named, the MCP face/charter text, search grammar docs.\n- **Dispatch shape:** Grok authors, opencode is the single review seat, and the debate happens as PR-comment back-and-forth until both settle (the human's ruling on all three points, 2026-08-19).","created":"2026-08-19T11:01:59-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:36-04:00","custom":{"from":"#246 (the human's ruling 2026-08-19)","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/3f70317c","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/266"}}
{"id":"dev-server-random-port","parent":"infra-build","ord":"a5","title":"A dev server never squats the production port — port 0 by default, fixed ports are a deploy's explicit word","done":"2026-08-19T19:28:23-04:00","desc":"Two field incidents in one night, same defect class.\n\n- **(1)** a dev instance bound `127.0.0.1:7714` — the production port — so the orchestrator's olai MCP answered with the dev vault's outlines all evening and the ledger was wrongly believed unreachable.\n- **(2)** the empty-trash lane's e2e dialed ANOTHER worktree's server through the shared `/tmp/olai-dev` convention and failed against a foreign bundle.\n- **Fix:** dev and e2e servers bind port 0 (OS-assigned), print the port at startup and write it to a per-worktree file the harness reads back; a fixed `--port` is something only a deploy passes explicitly.\n- Then a dev instance cannot squat production and two worktrees cannot dial each other.","created":"2026-08-19T11:02:04-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:36-04:00","custom":{"from":"2026-08-19 incident (the human's diagnosis)","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/82b1c543","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/264"}}
{"id":"private-dir-export","parent":"infra-upstream","ord":"aC","title":"Upstream: kolu exports its private-directory check and olai deletes its copy","done":"2026-08-19T16:55:36-04:00","desc":"Dispatched 2026-08-19 on the human's word while they read the conclusion of the third design debate (docs/lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-19.md, finding 3).\n\n- Two pull requests from one Grok work session:\n  1. kolu: export the `isPrivateOwnedDir` predicate from @kolu/surface's unix-socket module.\n  2. olai: bump the kolu version and delete `notPrivatelyOurs` (packages/server/src/lock.ts lines 318-334), which carries its own note: \"if upstream ever exports it, this function is the thing to delete\".\n- Signed by all three debaters across three rounds, and sized as a fix rather than a large piece of work.\n\nThe olai pull request was merged under the pipeline's own rule — a report with no deferred work skips the human's gate — after the orchestrator had wrongly parked it waiting for an approval nobody had asked for. Both reviews raised no objection, and CI was green at commit a1d29c02. Finding 3 is closed whole.\n\nThe kolu pull request was approved by the human on 2026-08-19; the olai side was in flight at that point.","created":"2026-08-19T13:49:45-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:11:35-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-grok","from":"lowy-electricity debate-2026-08-19 finding 3","merge-commit":["https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/0f551b2f","https://github.com/juspay/kolu/commit/1b3c20b5"],"pr-url":["https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/259","https://github.com/juspay/kolu/pull/2186"],"terminal":"0b26abe6-7c68-428a-ac42-d1a91019f734"}}
{"id":"surface-deltas-frame","parent":"infra-upstream","ord":"aD","title":"Upstream: kolu hands over what changed, so olai's deriving.ts can go","done":"2026-08-19T18:12:02-04:00","desc":"The headline of the third design debate (docs/lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-19.md, finding 1), ratified by the human 2026-08-19.\n\n- The change: one addition to the client half of @kolu/surface, with two parts shipping together.\n  - Merging a named key in place, with no copy of the whole dictionary and no walk over every entry — the measured biggest cost of typing into a large vault.\n  - A `fold({init, step})` method on handles that deliver deltas, gated by type.\n- Amendment from the survey of what kolu itself gains: also export `useCollectionDeltas` from the Solid barrel file.\n- `rev` stays, being part of the wire contract; @olai/format's patch function stays.\n- The specification, with signatures, semantics and edge cases: docs/lowy-electricity/surface-design-2026-08-19.md, section \"Finding 1\".\n- Beneficiaries, proven:\n  - olai deletes deriving.ts whole — outlines.ts hands frames straight to patch.\n  - drishti deletes its hand-written foldProcessDeltas; the paired drishti pull request is how the change gets adopted, not merely a re-green of CI.\n  - Four more drishti collections stop paying the silent copy.\n- Shipping: as a kolu pull request under the paired-drishti-PR gate plus the odu impact check — the change is additive, so the expected verdict is \"adoption opportunity\", to be confirmed by the required search — then olai bumps the version and the deletion is the installation.\n\nolai's pull request was approved by the human, with the pipeline waived given the change is a deletion: deriving.ts died whole, and kolu's own end-to-end benchmark records the improvement at up to 937 times, depending on frame shape. The deferred work was filed as the vaults-installed-deferrals node.\n\nkolu's pull request was approved by the human with both reviews raising no objection, and merged with `--admin` because kolu's base policy refuses self-approval. Remaining at that point: re-pin and merge drishti PR #143, then olai deletes deriving.ts at the version bump.\n\ndrishti's pull request deleted foldProcessDeltas and adopted the exported hook in the process table; olai's deletion pull request was in flight, in the vaults-installed work session.\n\nThe work ran in terminal f08e17da, kolu working tree surface-deltas-frame — one session, two pull requests, with drishti and odu handled along the way; dispatched 2026-08-19.","created":"2026-08-19T14:42:16-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:11:35-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-claude-opus","from":"lowy-electricity debate-2026-08-19 finding 1","merge-commit":["https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/b33fea13","https://github.com/juspay/kolu/commit/b4694c28","https://github.com/juspay/drishti/commit/185efde4"],"pr-url":["https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/263","https://github.com/juspay/kolu/pull/2187","https://github.com/juspay/drishti/pull/143"],"spec":"docs/lowy-electricity/surface-design-2026-08-19.md"}}
{"id":"surface-holders","parent":"infra-upstream","ord":"aE","title":"Upstream: the framework says when the last reader of a key leaves, so holding.ts can go","done":"2026-08-19T18:12:03-04:00","desc":"Finding 2 of the third design debate (docs/lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-19.md), ratified by the human 2026-08-19.\n\n- The change: one optional member on kolu's `CollectionHandlerDeps` — `holders?: (key) => Effect<unknown, never, Scope>`.\n  - Run via `Stream.unwrap` inside each reader's own get-stream scope, before `readOne`. That pull order is part of the contract, and holding.ts's test moves upstream to become the framework's own assertion.\n  - Closing the scope is the release. It never uses the error channel: a defect crashes that one subscription loudly, with no silently degraded \"unheld\" state.\n  - When the member is absent, the code path is byte-identical to today's.\n- Specification: docs/lowy-electricity/surface-design-2026-08-19.md, section \"Finding 2\".\n- This is where the problem already blew up: the sixteen-path LRU cache of PR #229.\n- olai deletes holding.ts and its test whole; runtime.ts says `holders: bodies.held`; bodies.ts stays entirely; the client-side map of askers stays out of scope, a separate axis that has already been ruled on.\n- odu's log store is a proven second consumer, and will adopt it at its next version bump.\n- Same shipping gates as the deltas-frame change, and ranked below it by the debate, being a younger idea with one consumer.\n\nolai's pull request: holding.ts and its test died whole; runtime.ts now says `holders: bodies.held`; the pull-order assertion was verified to be living upstream before the deletion.\n\nkolu's pull request was approved by the human with both reviews raising no objection, and needed one round of conflict resolution after PR #2187 landed, resolved by merging master at commit 59cc7dcd. Remaining at that point: merge drishti PR #144, then olai deletes holding.ts at the version bump.\n\nThe drishti pull request was closed as a no-op — PR #143 landed first carrying the same version, so there was nothing to adopt; the review proved by search that the impact on drishti was nil.\n\nSame work session as surface-deltas-frame (terminal f08e17da) — a second pull request from a second branch, opened after the first.","created":"2026-08-19T14:42:26-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:11:35-04:00","custom":{"from":"lowy-electricity debate-2026-08-19 finding 2","merge-commit":["https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/b33fea13","https://github.com/juspay/kolu/commit/f648f0a2"],"pr-url":["https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/263","https://github.com/juspay/kolu/pull/2188","https://github.com/juspay/drishti/pull/144"],"spec":"docs/lowy-electricity/surface-design-2026-08-19.md"}}
{"id":"debate3-claim-tests","parent":"infra-tests","ord":"a7","title":"Pin three promises as tests (from design debate #3)","done":"2026-08-24T17:36:52-04:00","desc":"Three promises the code makes, to be pinned as tests:\n(a) Address recognition has one door: addressIn delegates to routeIn, and nothing outside routes.ts recognizes an address.\n(b) Every call to createArrival keeps a literal `import()` specifier, because the bundler reads those statically; today that rule exists only as a comment.\n(c) Nothing outside holding.ts and runtime.ts spells the get-tag hold; this test is expected to die together with the surface-holders change, and its name should say so.\n\nOne small pull request. Recorded in docs/lowy-electricity/debate-2026-08-19.md, finding 4.\n\nMerge once the review has been applied and CI is green.","created":"2026-08-19T14:42:35-04:00","changed":"2026-08-27T19:11:35-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-pi","brief":"briefs/d3c.md","dispatched":"2026-08-24T16:45:00-04:00","from":"lowy-electricity debate-2026-08-19 finding 4","merge":"merge-auto","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/de40d859","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/370","rescope-2026-08-24":"roadmap review: claim (c) died as designed — surface-holders shipped in #263 (holding.ts deleted whole; the hold is bodies.ts:121-192's refcount handed to the framework). Two claims remain live and unpinned — (a) and (b) name addressIn/routeIn/createArrival, none tested in claims.test.ts, though addressIn already delegates (address.ts:64) and the menu half of (b) is covered by the chunk sweeps (claims.test.ts:359,394)","worktree":".worktrees/debate3-claim-tests"}}
{"id":"web-testlib-face","parent":"infra-tests","ord":"a6","title":"@olai/web gets a ./testlib export for the e2e suite","done":"2026-08-24T18:05:58-04:00","desc":"- packages/tests imports sixteen @olai/web/src/client files by package name while the manifest declares exports: \"None.\" — both can't be true.\n- Fix: a narrow ./testlib face (the convention format/git/log/ops already carry), with the manifest sentence rewritten in the same diff.\n- From debate #3, finding 5; the one-line ./testids bandage was considered and rejected.\n\n**merge** — on review folded + green CI","created":"2026-08-19T14:42:43-04:00","changed":"2026-08-24T18:05:58-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-pi","brief":"briefs/wtf.md","count-2026-08-24":"roadmap review: the trespass GREW — packages/tests now imports NINETEEN distinct @olai/web/src/client files (was sixteen at filing): backlinks/way, blocked, chat/completion, chat/near, chat/refs, clock, edit/draft, file/kinds, file/making, layout/prefs, longPress, settings/alerts, settings/density, settings/done, settings/hiddenOutlines, testids, theme/css, theme/palettes, theme/sizes. And the manifest tells TWO lies now: \"//exports\": \"None.\" plus \"the one thing imported across a package boundary is testids.ts\" — the same diff must rewrite both","dispatched":"2026-08-24T16:45:00-04:00","from":"lowy-electricity debate-2026-08-19 finding 5","merge":"merge-auto","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/42987d90","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/372","worktree":".worktrees/web-testlib-face"}}
{"id":"e2e-earn-browser","parent":"infra-tests","ord":"a5","title":"The e2e suite sheds what a browser doesn't earn — ~150 of 875 scenarios cut on the audit","done":"2026-08-19T22:34:25-04:00","desc":"The human's principle, distilled: an e2e scenario must EARN the browser.\n- Cut categories from the audit: (a) ~67 unit-test-shaped (a unit test already pins the law — filter grammar ×15, move_to_picker ×7, an_external_agent ×14…); (b) ~36 trivial/static render assertions; (c) ~34 one-law-many-doors permutations (keep one representative door); (d) ~14 pixel/geometry pins; (e) a few obsolete (the connection scenarios the offline-overlay ruling replaces are left for THAT PR to rewrite).\n- Every cut must verify its claimed unit-test overlap first; an unpinned claim gets its unit test in the same commit, never a bare delete.\n- The PR also writes the principle into packages/tests/README.md so it binds future authors, and records e2e wall time before/after.\n- KEEP class (earns the browser): stacking via elementFromPoint, real drag/touch, live-wire (watcher edits, reconnects, server death), multi-tab races, CSP/iframe sealing.\n\n**pr** — suite 875→717 scenarios, e2e ~3m32s→~3m7s; principle written into packages/tests/README.md","created":"2026-08-19T20:50:58-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:36-04:00","custom":{"agent":"agent-grok","from":"the human 2026-08-19 (audit commissioned in chat; dispatch + merge pre-approved)","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/c7806133","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/269"}}
{"id":"olai-service-sigterm","parent":"infra-server","ord":"a2","title":"olai.service dies by outside SIGTERM after hours up — twice in one night, the ledger goes dark each time","done":"2026-08-20T10:34:15-04:00","desc":"Observed twice while the service ran the pinned binary /nix/store/ylxg…-olai:\n- 23:06 EDT: exit 130 after 2h17m up (journal: received SIGTERM); ledger dark 105 min until the orchestrator restarted it.\n- 06:01 EDT: exit 130 after 5h09m up (journal: received SIGTERM); restarted within the hour.\n- **Mechanism (corrected 2026-08-20 from the live unit):** the unit DID carry `Restart=on-failure` — beside `SuccessExitStatus=130`, which declares the SIGTERM exit a success, so on-failure never fired. At both deaths the journal shows `received SIGTERM` with NO systemd `Stopping`/`Stopped` (the deliberate 20:49 / 08:12 restarts log `Stopped`): something signalled the process directly, in nix-daemon-heavy windows while overnight lanes ran e2e/CI.\n- **DONE 2026-08-20 — #280 (Grok, merged aef63ec76):** `Restart=always` + `RestartSec=1s`, `SuccessExitStatus=130` kept (systemd never restarts a `systemctl stop`, so deliberate stops stay deliberate; a stray SIGTERM now costs ~1s). Proven on transient units without touching the live service; check.nix asserts it; running.md describes it; RCA at docs/RCA/2026-08-20-olai-service-sigterm.md. Darwin already restarted a 130 (`SuccessfulExit=false`).\n- **Sender: unknown.** Every kill path in this repo and in the odu/kolu tooling was read and ruled out in the RCA's table (the e2e harness SIGKILLs its own child; wire/evidence scripts kill `$!`; `just serve` kills its own group; kolu dev-clean checks a state-root manifest; nix builds are PID-namespaced). If it recurs, the unit comes back and the journal's `received SIGTERM` without `Stopped` still names an outside signal.\n- **Third death, 11:54:18 EDT, before the deploy:** same shape (received SIGTERM, `Consumed … over 3h 42min`, no Stopping/Stopped, exit 130 = success, NRestarts=0) under the still-old unit started 08:12. Timing note for the sender hunt: within a minute of the orchestrator spawning reactivity PR 3's Kolu terminal and its Claude Code session booting (11:53–11:54); the earlier two also fell in lane-spawn/CI windows. Ledger dark 4 min — the human deployed at 11:58.\n- **Deployed 2026-08-20 11:58** (home-manager switch by the human): the live unit now reads Restart=always / RestartSec=1s / SuccessExitStatus=130 on /nix/store/i2v7hgc1…-olai. The next outside SIGTERM is the proof; `NRestarts` will say.","created":"2026-08-20T06:51:51-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:36-04:00","custom":{"from":"the orchestrator's overnight observations 2026-08-19→20"}}
{"id":"archive-migrate-vault","parent":"infra-model","ord":"a2","title":"Migrate this vault's two leftover Archive.olai files into _olai/Trash.olai — the one trash holds what the archives held","done":"2026-08-20T13:46:02-04:00","desc":"The human's ask, 2026-08-20 13:08: \"did we migrate the old file to new file path? if not do it.\" #266 (olai-convention-dir) shipped the one trash with the 2026-08-19 ruling \"leave-and-stop-reading, no migration\" — so `docs/Archive.olai` (25 records) and `docs/orchestrator/Archive.olai` (13) were still on disk, dormant. Root cause of there being TWO: the pre-#266 rule put an archive \"beside the outline it left\", one per directory — the orchestrator's 2026-08-19 put-away of the What's-new lane from `orchestrator/lanes.olai` minted the second.\n- **DONE 2026-08-20 — #291 (Grok, merged afa76be11; review waived by the human).** One `_olai/Trash.olai` of 40 records: outermost signposts `roadmap.olai` and `orchestrator/lanes.olai`, then the archives' ancestor-title chains, then the records untouched (git sees a rename of docs/Archive.olai plus the 13 appended). Both Archive.olai files gone. Proven through the product's faces on a copy: validator ok (49 files), trash page draws both groups, `is:trashed` 40/40, default search misses them, `untrash_node` resolves a sample from each group by the recorded chain without overrides. The migration script ran once and was not shipped; format.md's leftover-archive rule is unchanged.\n- **Open question for the human (from the PR body):** should the PRODUCT offer this wrapping to every vault that still holds leftover `Archive.olai` files? Not built here.\n\n**merge** — on the human's 'do it'","created":"2026-08-20T13:08:58-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T13:01:36-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-20","merge":"merge-human"}}
{"id":"kolu-watch-ignore-self","parent":"infra-upstream","ord":"aF","title":"Upstream: kolu watch gets ignore flags, per-line flush, and a heartbeat #upstream","done":"2026-08-21T21:43:09-04:00","desc":"- Three changes in one PR (kolu#2194):\n  - `--ignore-self` and repeatable `--ignore <id>` — fail-open muting, born from a self-watching feedback loop.\n  - Bug fix: the event stream now flushes per line even when piped (piped output used to emit nothing, silently killing supervision pipelines).\n  - `--heartbeat <interval>` — a timestamped alive line, so a watcher's silence is falsifiable.\n- Fixes verified live from a deployed branch build. The human took the PR over with their own Claude; the orchestrator stands down.\n\n**kolu-pr** — (2026-08-21 21:35) — --ignore/--ignore-self, per-line flush when piped, --heartbeat; verified live on the production build by the orchestrator (see supervision-watcher), then merged by the human","created":"2026-08-21T08:16:58-04:00","changed":"2026-08-21T21:43:09-04:00","custom":{"from":"the human 2026-08-21, from the sixth-lapse aftermath","merge-commit":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/commit/aadc3845","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/kolu/pull/2194"}}
